# github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2+incompatible in go.mod and pkg/plugins/go.mod
# CVE-2026-34040: AuthZ plugin bypass via oversized request bodies (affects Docker daemon).
# Grafana does NOT run a Docker daemon or AuthZ plugins — it uses docker only as an indirect
# client-side dependency. The fix version (v29.3.1) does NOT exist as a Go module
# (pkg.go.dev shows "no known fixed" for github.com/docker/docker). Cannot upgrade.
CVE-2026-34040

# github.com/grafana/tempo (pseudo-version v1.5.1-*) — CVE-2026-21728, CVE-2026-28377
# The fix requires upgrading to github.com/grafana/tempo/v2 (major module path change).
# This is a CODE MIGRATION, not a simple bump: all import paths in pkg/tsdb/tempo/*.go
# must be changed from "github.com/grafana/tempo/..." to "github.com/grafana/tempo/v2/...".
# Additionally, both CVEs are in the Tempo SERVER (DoS via large queries, S3 key disclosure);
# Grafana uses tempo only as a CLIENT via protobuf bindings (pkg/tempopb) — the vulnerable
# server code paths are not in the execute path for Grafana.
# Tracked separately for a dedicated migration PR.
CVE-2026-21728
CVE-2026-28377

# github.com/openfga/openfga v1.8.13 — CVE-2026-40293, CVE-2026-41131
# NOT FIXABLE via dependency bump on release-1.7 due to a k8s major version incompatibility:
#   openfga v1.14.0+ (the first fix for CVE-2026-40293) requires k8s.io/api v0.35.x,
#   but the Grafana codebase uses k8s.io/apiserver v0.33.3 which is built against
#   sigs.k8s.io/structured-merge-diff/v4. k8s v0.35.x switched to v6, and the two
#   type systems are incompatible — mixing them causes a compile error in pkg/aggregator,
#   pkg/apiserver, and grafana-app-sdk. Fixing this requires a full k8s v0.33 → v0.35
#   migration with source code changes (out of scope for a security patch PR).
# CVE-2026-41131 only affects openfga v1.14.0 specifically; since v1.14.x cannot be used,
#   this CVE is also not applicable.
# Workaround: disable the openfga playground (--playground-enabled=false).
# Tracked in ACM-33102 as CANNOT_FIX / Requires k8s migration.
CVE-2026-40293
CVE-2026-41131

